    "updated_at": "2023-12-19T15:35:23Z",
    "body": "There's some text here https://www.w3.org/TR/css-contain-2/#skips-its-contents that describes it. It uses _should_ language though instead of _must_, but these elements must not paint or respond to hit-testing or be focusable for example. \r\n\r\nFor this particular issue, I would imagine showPicker should not show anything, and perhaps that can be documented in https://www.w3.org/TR/css-contain-2/#cv-notes -- as an example, there's already text there about, among other things, that skipped contents doesn't contribute to innerText",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
