    "created_at": "2023-12-19T19:46:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-12-19T19:46:35Z",
    "body": "I'd be a little worried about content-visibility auto, which when it's not relevant to the user skips its contents. Specifically, the contents contained within this are still discoverable by find in page, for example. But does find in page require rendering? I'm not sure.\r\n\r\nSo I'm ok with the language as you suggest, I would just want to double check whether \"element is being rendered\" is used in contexts where a skipped element should have its rendering done",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
